A||N||10||FIERO1985||Having Many Problems||||4||
Z||000000||FIERO1985||11-25-2000||05:50 PM||||I have been having problems driving at 45-75 mph when the car all the sudden cuts out and the tach will bottom out and the car will plain die! then will cut back in. within the week the car died completely and will only crank. I have reason to believe it is eith a control module or possibly a fuel delivery prob. if you have suggestions or pinpoints to check please respond!<BR>thanks<BR>Dan||||reg||4
Z||000001||strdream||11-25-2000||06:18 PM||||With so little to go by I would guess Ignition module first.  A quick test is to give it a sniff of starting fluid while cranking.  If it responds it's a fuel system problem.  If not... look at ignition.<P>Ross  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FIERO1985||11-25-2000||08:28 PM||||I went out just a little while after setting for a while and it fire up as usual within 1 crank but I have reason to believe I heard that there is a module the when it gets hot it will cause the engine to quit whenever it goes bad. I am not sure but I also heard it is located under the distributor?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000003||Old Lar||11-25-2000||08:43 PM||||The ignition module is located under the distributor cap.  Not knowing much about your car, it could be the distributor itself.  I had mine replaced after 13 years, the car ran ok, but the inside of the distributor was very corroded.  So if the distributor and module are original equipment, it may be time for a change, as well as wires and spark plugs.<P>The distributor does get warm in its location on the engine.||||reg||3
Z||000004||Jackalrr||11-25-2000||08:56 PM||||I had the same problem. It was not the ignition module, although I did end up replacing it, the distributer cap and the ignition coil. The problem went away and then came back. The plugs were fireing but it just wouldn't start. There was no fuel problem either. <P>Once every other week this would happen and it could be temporarly fixed by tapping on the distributer cap and ignition coil with a hammer. I just replaced the pick up coil and I am almost 100% sure that was it. About a week has gone by with no problem yet. Email me if you want specifics.<P>Hope it helps,<BR>-Charlie<BR>-----<BR>jackalrr@cinci.rr.com||||reg||1
Z||000005||FIERO1985||11-25-2000||11:18 PM||||I have replaced the plugs and wires and also the coil in the past 3-4 months but I also have owned the car for 1 1/2 years and I have not replaced the ign. module nor the distributor the engine has many mods and all I can see of this problem is when it is hot and traveling at a set speed but not when accelling the car will die. But when it is setting an extended period the car will run fine when warmmed up a bit!<P>Dan<P>------------------<BR>Dan||||reg||5
Z||000006||maninblack||11-26-2000||06:23 AM||||mine just quit on me last sat nite.end up it is the ign module, but the dis. cap<BR>looks pretty burnt ,so i replaced that too.||||reg||1
Z||000007||FIERO1985||11-26-2000||10:46 AM||||Ok :I am going to have the ign. mod. checked at auto zone and probably replace it then I will check the distrib. cap and will replace if it needs it and I will return if it does the trick!<P>Thanks<BR>Dan||||reg||10
Z||000008||DavidHenshaw||11-26-2000||12:00 PM||||I had the same problem. Turned out to be the distributor itself. The insides of the distributor were very rusty and the small copper coil inside the distributor appeared to be burned. My ignition module checked out ok but when I purchased the new distributor a new ignition module was part of the package.<BR>I've put on 2,000 miles since with no problem.<P>In addition to a new distributor I also repalaced distributor cap, rotor, coil, plug wires and spark plugs. Might as well do it right.<P>Dave<P>86 GT<P> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||FIERO1985||11-26-2000||03:57 PM||||thank you all for the replys I checked and replaced the ign module and it seems to be running fine and the test will be this week if anything else goes wrong in those lines I will replace the distrib. components and for now I dont need to!<P>Thank you all<BR>Dan||||reg||1
Z||000010||RiceBurner515||11-26-2000||09:26 PM||||were you working the engine hard or going at high speeds for a long period of time? Cuz i used to have a Camaro and that is the same thing that happened to me...it was a bearing in the engine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  didn't bother to fix and jumked it....then went out and bought a 85SE 5spd for $300, a steal!||||reg||1
